  <!-- ===== FAQ (bê thiết kế y hệt J-1, nội dung riêng visa 407 Úc) ===== -->
  <section class="faq-section" id="faq">
    <div class="container faq-container">
      <h2 class="faq-mega">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>What is visa 407, and how does SBB's Australia path program work?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Visa 407 is <strong>Australia's Training visa</strong>, which lets you go to Australia to learn a trade and build real skills at an Australian business in the field you are pursuing.</p>
            <p>SBB handles the whole journey: skills assessment, foundation and language preparation, placement through our partner Australian Internships, then completing the sponsorship and visa paperwork for you.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>Who is the 407 program for? What do I need to get started?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>It suits students, recent graduates or people already working who are targeting one of the fields our partner is currently hosting.</p>
            <p>Basic requirements: 18 or older, a study background or experience in the right field, and English good enough for the job. Each field has its own requirements; click each card in the What You'll Do section for the details.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>My English isn't strong yet, can I still go on 407?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Yes, if you start early. Most fields require good to strong English (equivalent to IELTS 5.5), while Early Childhood and Aged Care need IELTS 6.0.</p>
            <p>The SBB path builds applied English in parallel with preparing your profile, practising hard until you are confident enough before going to Australia.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>What fields does 407 place students into in Australia?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Our partner Australian Internships hosts many areas across Australia: <strong>Professional, Hospitality, STEM, Stipend, Virtual, Early Childhood Education and Aged &amp; Disability Care</strong>.</p>
            <p>Specific spots depend on the field and hiring timing. You can see each area's requirements and duration in the What You'll Do section.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>How long does the journey take from the start to landing in Australia?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>The journey follows clear steps, not sign up and wait:</p>
            <ul class="faq-stats">
              <li><b>1 · Initial assessment:</b> see whether your profile is truly a fit for the Australia path.</li>
              <li><b>2 · Foundation building:</b> mindset, conduct and language skills.</li>
              <li><b>3 · Placement through partners:</b> Australian Internships finds a suitable position.</li>
              <li><b>4 · Review &amp; departure:</b> complete the sponsorship, apply for visa 407 and go to Australia.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The timeline depends on each person's starting point. You will get a roadmap with specific milestones during your consultation.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>Do you get paid going to Australia on the 407 stream?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>It depends on the field. Areas like Hospitality, Early Childhood and Aged Care are <strong>paid positions</strong>; Stipend comes with a monthly allowance; while Professional, STEM and Virtual are usually unpaid positions.</p>
            <p>The exact rate depends on the position and the host business. What matters most is that you learn a real trade and build international experience.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>Roughly how much does the 407 program cost?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>The cost depends on the field, the duration and the position in Australia, so instead of a generic number, SBB <strong>breaks down each item transparently</strong> right in the consultation.</p>
            <p>The program is split into stages with flexible support options, so families do not have to shoulder the entire cost right at the start.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>Does SBB handle the sponsor and visa? Who is Australian Internships?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Yes. SBB is the <strong>exclusive representative in Vietnam</strong> of Australian Internships, one of Australia's leading training and internship host organisations.</p>
            <p>The partner handles the business placement and visa 407 sponsorship; SBB stays with you throughout the preparation and visa application.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>Visa 407 is a training stream, so will I be sent over as cheap labour?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>No. Visa 407 is designed for <strong>learning a trade and building real skills</strong>, with a clear training plan at the host business.</p>
            <p>That is why SBB prepares your profile and field direction carefully from the start, so you go on the right stream and truly learn a trade.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>What if I'm refused a visa or change my plans midway?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>SBB prepares the paperwork and interview carefully to maximise your chances of approval.</p>
            <p>Situations like an unfavourable profile or a change of plans all have clear options and policies, discussed transparently from the start so you feel secure about your rights.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

